{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bfeted3ra","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WFRdom8gyzM3YJFQfYzQk5","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/06447d70-aaa8-4d2b-8043-b355a610ecf8/tasks/bfeted3ra.output","summary":"Background command \"C=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3_repair_1\ncat << 'EOF' > $C/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `rule_built_tally_switch_triplet` (running heads-minus-tails tally judged by closeness of its span to a personal expected span with person-specific, length-scaled sensitivity; switching judged by closeness to a shared ideal rate with person-specific weight; a reward for variety of three-flip chunks; a penalty on sequences built by a copying or mirror rule; a personal left/right lean). The one change: people differ in how much they attend to the pattern structure of a sequence — each person has their own pattern sensitivity, a single trait that scales both structural cues together (chunk variety and the rule-built penalty), so some people reliably reject recycled-chunk and rule-built sequences while others barely notice them and judge only by tally and switching. This addresses the critique (surviving FDR) that participants differ in how often they agree with the majority more than the incumbent allows, locating that heterogeneity in pattern perception rather than in decision noise or lapses.\nEOF\necho person_pattern_sensitivity_rule_built > $C/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nC=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3_repair_1/candidate.py\"\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/rule_built_tally_switch_triplet.py\").read()\nsrc=src.replace('''\"\"\"Tally span ideal + ideal switching rate + triplet variety + rule-built penalty.\n\nRefinement of `tally_span_switch_ideal_triplet_variety`: people keep a running\nheads-minus-tails tally and judge a sequence random by how close its span is\nto their own expected span (person-specific, length-scaled sensitivity,\npersonal left/right lean), judge switching by closeness to an ideal switching\nrate (person-specific weight) and reward variety of three-flip chunks. The one\nchange: a sequence visibly built by a construction rule -- a short unit copied\nthroughout (HTHTHTHT, HHTHHT) or a reversed, face-swapped mirror of itself\n(HHHTHTTT, HHHHTTTT) -- looks designed, a single shared penalty.\n\"\"\"''','''\"\"\"Rule-built tally/switch/triplet judgement with person-specific pattern sensitivity.\n\nRefinement of `rule_built_tally_switch_triplet`: people keep a running\nheads-minus-tails tally and judge a sequence random by how close its span is\nto their own expected span (person-specific, length-scaled sensitivity,\npersonal left/right lean), judge switching by closeness to an ideal switching\nrate (person-specific weight), reward variety of three-flip chunks and\npenalise sequences built by a copying or mirror rule. The one change: people\ndiffer in how much they attend to pattern structure -- a single person-specific\ngain scales both structural cues (chunk variety and the rule-built penalty).\n\"\"\"''')\nold='''    # Person-specific left/right'''\nnew='''    # The change: person-specific pattern sensitivity scaling both structural cues\n    # (median 1, so gamma and rho remain the typical person's weights).\n    sigma_pat = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_pat\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_pat = pm.Normal(\"z_pat\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=N_SLOTS)\n    pat = pm.math.exp(sigma_pat * z_pat)\n\n    # Person-specific left/right'''\nassert old in src; src=src.replace(old,new)\nold='''        + gamma * trip_diff\n        - rho * rule_diff'''\nnew='''        + pat[participant_id] * (gamma * trip_diff - rho * rule_diff)'''\nassert old in src; src=src.replace(old,new)\nopen(C,\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $C --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"f1371157-bc1f-4c31-bf52-870eb57c4140","session_id":"06447d70-aaa8-4d2b-8043-b355a610ecf8"}
